<feature_description encoding="literal-redacted">
# sh-to-py B4: external-agent launcher framework

Part of the sh-to-py bash-to-Python migration (umbrella tracking issue links all parts).

**Goal**: Extend python/agents.py into the full external-agent launcher framework: waterfall tiers, auth probing, model args, prompt wrapping, usage capture, degraded-tool posture.

**Absorbs (approx lines)**: scripts/lib-external-launcher-common.sh (853), lib-codex-launcher-common (37), lib-cursor-launcher-common (569), lib-cursor-auth (217), cursor-auth-flags (57), cursor-wrap-prompt (40), agent-model-args (183), read-claude-model (35), external-tool-registry (70), launch-codex-ci (264), launch-codex-exec (250), launch-cursor-ci (254), launch-claude-ci (280), launch-claude-review (225), launch-claude-subprocess (309), run-external-agent (362), lib-failed-agent-stderr-tail (251), parse-codex-usage (129), degraded-tools-gate (181; 6 .md refs).

**Notes**: calls B2 functions for token-record appends and B3 functions for tool-failure batch capture (closing the python/README Phase-7 deferral). launch-codex-implement / launch-cursor-implement stay with C4b (implementer-specific manifest contracts) but reuse this framework. docs/external-reviewers.md describes the integration surface.

**Dependencies (wired natively via /block-issue)**: F1, F2, B2, B3.

**Definition of done**: importable functions; CLI verbs in python/cli.py; direct call-site cutover (no shims); pytest replaces harness coverage (test-launch-review.sh stays with C1a; test-lib-external-launcher-common.sh and test-run-external-agent.sh port here); absorbed bash + harnesses deleted; stale-reference sweep; make lint + py-lint + py-test green.

</feature_description>


